From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Use the configured library directory in pkg-config metadata
Source: https://github.com/kloetzl/libmurmurhash/blob/8b7c9bf3ed1b8f83e5265c84a2cad5c1d6bb1d69/libmurmurhash.pc.in
Original-License: LicenseRef-Public-Domain
Applies-To: Libmurmurhash 1.6; openEuler riscv64 /usr/lib64 layout
Upstream-Status: Downstream layout compatibility only; not submitted upstream
Root-Cause: The upstream template hardcodes /lib instead of the configured libdir
Removal-Condition: Official upstream template substitutes @libdir@ correctly

Keep configured Makefile installation and pkg-config libdir consistent.
No runtime, test, fixture, license, shared or static feature is changed.
The complete original template is preserved in installed source evidence.
GNU patch --fuzz=0 interprets the previous two-leading/one-trailing context
hunk as ending at EOF and rejects this longer template. Use a zero-context
single-line hunk, guarded by the complete original template SHA-256 in %prep.
This preserves the exact same one-line layout correction without fuzzy matching.

diff --git a/libmurmurhash.pc.in b/libmurmurhash.pc.in
--- a/libmurmurhash.pc.in
+++ b/libmurmurhash.pc.in
@@ -3 +3 @@
-libdir=${exec_prefix}/lib
+libdir=@libdir@
